<Defs>

	<ThingDef ParentName="CGF1_MWP_LMG_MagFed_T1">
		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type74_LMG_</defName>
		<label>Type 74 LMG</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x39mm. 30-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.

The Type 74 is a Chinese indigenous light machine gun that bares a resemblance to the Soviet RPK (albeit sharing nothing mechanically.) It was designed and produced in the 1970s in order to provide a magazine/drum-fed machine gun to PLA forces which at that point lacked such a weapon, but the Type 74's design was quite lackluster and never accepted for military service. However, some components of the design would survive to be used in the later Type 81 weapon system.</description>
